      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T22:37:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: monitors-\u003elen * sizeof(struct wrapfd_monitor) can overflow unsigned long if monitors-\u003elen is very large. Since kcalloc handles overflow internally but copy_from_user does not, this can lead to a heap buffer overflow in the loop below.\n\nAlso, there is no upper limit on monitors-\u003elen, allowing a user to potentially exhaust kernel memory.\n\nisaacmanjarres: Not sure about the last part, but the rest of it seems reasonable. Also, if we do allow a large number, should we be using `kvmalloc()`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2074,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2074,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "22dcbefae3d64d55ac58dbad4c0a623fdf3aa382",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
