      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T22:37:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: This makes poll() non-idempotent. Standard poll should be level-triggered and not consume the state. If multiple threads call poll(), or if epoll is used in level-triggered mode, only the first call will see the event. \n\nFurthermore, if WRAPFD_DEV_IOC_QUERY_EVENTS returns with has_more\u003dtrue, subsequent polls will return 0 because this bit was already cleared here.\n\nIt should be:\nif (atomic_read(\u0026file_mon-\u003eevents_pending))\n    mask |\u003d (EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDNORM);",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2335,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2335,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "22dcbefae3d64d55ac58dbad4c0a623fdf3aa382",
